<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<request-parameters>
<!--
  D16 = "Compressed Mortality, 1979-1998" (ICD-9 era). Params matched to a
  captured working D16 web-UI request (Group Results By = Year, And By = ICD
  Chapter, Age-Adjusted Rate checked):
    B_1  = D16.V1          (Year)
    B_2  = D16.V2-level1   (ICD Chapter -- the coarse ~17-chapter roll-up)
    O_aar = aar_std + O_aar_enable = true   (age-adjusted; 2000 US std pop)
  COARSE ON PURPOSE -- chapter grain maps to the ICD-10 chapter roll-ups with
  no ICD-9 -> ICD-10 comparability crosswalk. A 113-list-equivalent breakdown
  is a separate, larger effort (see CLAUDE.md).
  Rounds 1-2 returned a bare "Processing Error"; the fix was the missing
  O_aar=aar_std (the checkbox alone isn't enough) plus leaving the location
  V_ fields BLANK -- CMF reads blank as "all of the United States"; the
  D192-style "Code '' isn't valid" rejection does not apply here.
  {{YEAR_LIST}} -> V_D16.V1. Response cells: year, chapter (label, h= depth),
  Deaths, Population, Crude Rate, Age-Adjusted Rate -> the same 6-col contract
  as the `icd10` era.
  Test: node --env-file=.env fetch.js --type=mortality --era=icd9 --years=1979-1985 --out=rows.json --dump
  On a 400: paste the <message> from pipeline/mortality_icd9_chapter.raw.xml.
-->
